{"id": "2026-08-15-news-heat-summer-ravages-swiss-beech-forests", "date": "2026-08-15", "stream": "news", "headline": "Heat summer ravages Swiss beech forests", "summary": "An IAP survey finds two-thirds of monitored beeches severely damaged in the 2026 heat summer, nearly triple 2018, as the Rhine and springs run dry.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/wissen/klimawandel/beispiellose-waldschaeden-der-schweizer-wald-steht-vor-einem-tiefgreifenden-wandel", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "science"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "The 2026 heat-and-drought summer is inflicting damage on Swiss forests that long-term monitors say they have never recorded, even as rivers and springs run dry. New field surveys by the Institut für angewandte Pflanzenbiologie (IAP — an applied-plant-biology institute that has monitored Swiss forest health for various cantons since 1974) found that in the beech stands it tracks, two-thirds of the trees are now severely damaged — browning, shedding leaves, or with badly thinned crowns — nearly three times the count after the previous record-heat summer of 2018. The institute's Sabine Braun, who inspects roughly 12,000 trees across 23 cantons each year, said leaves are now drying on the branch and even green ones are \"getting sunburnt\" — a phenomenon she says she has not seen in 42 years of measurements. Because only about a quarter of the beeches badly hit in 2018 survived, and it is the accumulation of dry years that kills, researchers warn the beech — Switzerland's commonest broadleaf — could all but vanish from the northwest. The drought is visible elsewhere too: Basel's Rhine passenger ferry \"Wild Maa\" has been beached because the river is too weak to run it, and in peripheral regions springs have dried up, forcing water to be trucked in by tank.", "why": "forest composition, drinking-water supply and even summer traditions are shifting inside a single season, and the survey turns an abstract \"hot summer\" into a measured, hard-to-reverse ecological change on the ground. (SRF, 15 Aug 2026; low-Rhine impacts", "thread_id": "2026-08-15-news-heat-summer-ravages-swiss-beech-forests", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-15", "event_date": "2026-08-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Switzerland", "IAP", "Rhine", "Basel"]}
{"id": "2026-08-15-news-swiss-motion-pushes-local-tech-procurement", "date": "2026-08-15", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss motion pushes local tech procurement", "summary": "Vaud Green MP Sophie Michaud Gigon will defend a motion urging Bern to favour Swiss and EU digital suppliers over US ones, backed by Proton and Infomaniak.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/articles/et-si-la-suisse-privilegiait-ses-propres-entreprises-tech-pour-ses-achats-de-services-numeriques-un-vif-debat-s-amorce-a-berne", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "tech"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "A Vaud Green MP will ask federal commissioners next week to steer Switzerland's public IT spending toward Swiss and European suppliers rather than US ones. National Councillor Sophie Michaud Gigon (Greens, Vaud) told Le Temps she will defend a motion in the powerful Commission for Economic Affairs and Taxation on 17 or 18 August, arguing that Bern spends hundreds of millions of francs a year on digital services — often American — that Swiss firms could provide, and that this contradicts the \"digital sovereignty\" strategy the Confederation itself adopted in 2025. Swiss providers Proton and Infomaniak back the text. Motions of this kind have failed before, and the proposal now has to survive the commission and both chambers, so it is a starting pressure point rather than a settled rule.", "why": "it puts a concrete, procurement-level lever behind the much-repeated \"digital sovereignty\" slogan — the kind of measure that would actually redirect money and reduce dependence on US cloud vendors, of direct interest to anyone working in Swiss software.", "thread_id": "2026-08-15-news-swiss-motion-pushes-local-tech-procurement", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-15", "event_date": "2026-08-17", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Sophie Michaud Gigon", "Switzerland", "Proton", "Infomaniak"]}
{"id": "2026-08-15-news-swissmedic-flags-hospital-cleanroom-failures", "date": "2026-08-15", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swissmedic flags hospital cleanroom failures", "summary": "Swissmedic says hospital pharmacy cleanrooms often fail hygiene standards for preparing sterile drugs; the hospital association cites tight budgets.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/schweiz/hygienemaengel-in-spitaelern-swissmedic-die-reinraeume-sind-nicht-wirklich-reinraeume", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "health"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The Swiss medicines regulator says hospital cleanrooms — where sterile drugs are prepared — often fail to meet the hygiene standard their name implies. Swissmedic put it bluntly to SRF: \"the cleanrooms are not really cleanrooms,\" pointing to shortcomings in how hospital pharmacies prepare sterile preparations such as infusions and cytostatics. The hospital association acknowledged the need to act but pointed to tight budgets as a constraint on upgrades.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-08-15-news-swissmedic-flags-hospital-cleanroom-failures", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-15", "event_date": "2026-08-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Swissmedic", "Switzerland"]}
{"id": "2026-08-15-news-drc-ebola-outbreak-turns-deadliest-ever", "date": "2026-08-15", "stream": "news", "headline": "DRC Ebola outbreak turns deadliest ever", "summary": "The UN says the eastern DRC Bundibugyo Ebola outbreak has killed 2,184, one death every 30 minutes, and released another $30.5m in emergency funds.", "url": "https://news.un.org/feed/view/en/story/2026/08/1168148", "source_domain": "news.un.org", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["health", "world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The Ebola outbreak in eastern DR Congo has become the deadliest on record, with the UN reporting one death roughly every 30 minutes and releasing another $30.5 million in emergency funds. UN humanitarian chief Tom Fletcher said Friday 14 August that the Bundibugyo-strain outbreak — a species of Ebola virus, declared by DRC authorities on 15 May — has now killed 2,184 people, about 47% of confirmed cases, and that \"Ebola is winning.\" He allocated a further $30.5m from the UN's Central Emergency Response Fund on top of $24m already committed, and OCHA has deployed extra staff to the epicentre. The toll has roughly doubled since mid-July, when the pipeline last recorded it near 1,000, and about half the deaths have come in the most recent stretch; a race to deploy newer vaccines is under way.", "why": "a case-fatality rate near half and the fastest spread ever recorded mean the response is losing ground, with cross-border spillover risk in a conflict-hit region. (UN News, 15 Aug 2026; vaccine push", "thread_id": "2026-06-22-cyber-papers-ebola-cases-surpass-1-000-in-dr-congo-amid-viole", "first_seen_date": "2026-06-22", "event_date": "2026-08-14", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Ebola", "DR Congo", "OCHA", "Tom Fletcher"]}
{"id": "2026-08-15-news-israeli-strike-kills-seven-in-south-lebanon", "date": "2026-08-15", "stream": "news", "headline": "Israeli strike kills seven in south Lebanon", "summary": "An Israeli air strike on a house in Ansar killed seven, the deadliest attack in Lebanon since a June de-escalation with Hezbollah.", "url": "https://nna-leb.gov.lb/en/news/short/222452", "source_domain": "nna-leb.gov.lb", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics", "security"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "An Israeli air strike flattened a house in southern Lebanon early Saturday, killing seven people in what local reporting called the deadliest attack since a June de-escalation with Hezbollah. Lebanon's National News Agency said Civil Defence teams recovered the dead and wounded from the outskirts of Ansar, in the Nabatieh district, after a strike destroyed the building; Al Jazeera, citing state media, put the toll at seven killed and three wounded. NNA reported strikes intensifying overnight across the Ali al-Taher ridge and near Nabatieh al-Fawqa, including — for the first time since the two-month-old ceasefire — into the valley between Ansar and Zarariyeh. Israel's military said it was continuing operations.", "why": "it is the sharpest breach yet of the fragile June arrangement that had quieted the Israel–Hezbollah front, and pushes strikes deeper into southern Lebanon than at any point since the truce.", "thread_id": "2026-08-06-news-israel-strikes-south-lebanon-amid-rome-talks", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-06", "event_date": "2026-08-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Israel", "Lebanon", "Hezbollah", "Nabatieh"]}
{"id": "2026-08-15-news-seoul-offers-talks-to-end-korean-war", "date": "2026-08-15", "stream": "news", "headline": "Seoul offers talks to end Korean War", "summary": "South Korea's president Lee Jae Myung proposed talks with the North to replace the 1953 armistice with a peace settlement and curb its nuclear programme.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/8/15/south-koreas-president-wants-talks-with-north-to-end-korean-war", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics", "world"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "South Korea's president has proposed formally ending the Korean War, offering talks with the North to replace the 1953 armistice with a peace settlement. President Lee Jae Myung said dialogue could turn the armistice — which halted the 1950–53 war but never legally ended it — into a durable \"peace regime,\" and argued engagement could also help curb Pyongyang's advancing nuclear programme. It is an opening offer with no sign yet of a Northern response.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-08-15-news-seoul-offers-talks-to-end-korean-war", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-15", "event_date": "2026-08-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["South Korea", "North Korea", "Lee Jae Myung"]}
